@startuml frontend_product_boundary
' Source baseline: 7b655487df80685187ed0193f6578060615f7d43.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/App.vue (createSession, resumeSession, submit, product shell).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (useRuntimeApi, requestRaw, consumeSse).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts (projectRuntimeEvents).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java.
' Observed behavior: the product shell hides credentials and protocol fields, but its transitional adapter still calls Runtime V1 directly.
' Target-only design: the production UI uses a public bridge; the mate-service Agent, Chat, Attachment, and public event contracts do not exist yet.
' Design reason: internal session identifiers, credentials, ETags, and raw SSE payloads must not cross the production browser boundary.

title CampusClaw product frontend boundary
left to right direction

actor "Campus user" as User
rectangle "Product frontend" as Frontend {
  component "Agent and chat workspace" as Workspace
  component "Product event projector" as Projector
  component "Direct runtime adapter\n(transition only)" as DirectAdapter
  component "Developer diagnostics\n(internal build only)" as Diagnostics
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Public chat API" as PublicApi
  component "Chat to session mapping" as Mapping
  component "Auth, policy, and event projection" as Policy
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "Session controllers" as Sessions
  component "Request-scoped SSE" as Stream
}

User --> Workspace : chat tasks
Workspace --> PublicApi : public HTTP and SSE
PublicApi --> Policy
Policy --> Mapping
Mapping --> Sessions : internal HTTP
Stream --> Policy : internal SSE events
Policy --> Projector : public safe events
Workspace ..> DirectAdapter : current integration
DirectAdapter ..> Sessions : internal HTTP and SSE
Diagnostics ..> Sessions : local diagnostics only

note bottom of Frontend
Product constraints:
- No Service URL or credential editor
- No raw session_id, ETag, JSON, or SSE frames
- Agent, chat, and attachment metadata use public resources
- Transitional direct adapter is not a production boundary
end note

note bottom of Mate
Security hardening:
- Terminate browser authentication
- Authorize each action
- Project internal errors and events
- Do not byte-forward internal SSE
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Observed internal contract:
- 11 Session Runtime operations
- One active execution per Session
- Persistent Entry history plus transient progress events
end note
@enduml

@startuml runtime_event_ui_projection
' Source baseline: 7b655487df80685187ed0193f6578060615f7d43.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts (projectRuntimeEvents, projectAssistantEvent, projectToolEvent).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (dispatchSseFrame, mergeRuntimeEvent, loadHistory).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/ComposerBox.vue (onKeydown, current follow-up mode).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventType.java (RuntimeEventType).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java (projectMessageStart, projectMessageUpdate, projectToolStart, projectToolEnd).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java (toHistoryEvent, toSseData).
' Product-reference evidence: ChatGPT.app webview/assets/app-initial-BCLYDefw.js (followUpQueueMode, K9s) and webview/assets/zh-CN-ByRVSIXt.js.
' Observed behavior: persistent entries and transient execution events share one request-scoped SSE response.
' Observed Codex behavior: desktop follow-up mode defaults to steer; a modifier submits one message with the inverse mode.
' Design reason: the UI projects protocol events into stable conversation objects and uses one current follow-up mode instead of two persistent choices.

title Runtime events to product UI projection
left to right direction

rectangle "Runtime event families" as Events {
  component "user.message" as UserEvent
  component "assistant.message.started\nassistant.message.delta\nassistant.message.completed" as AssistantEvents
  component "tool.execution.started\ntool.execution.completed\ntool.result" as ToolEvents
  component "session.status.idle\nstream.end\nstream.error" as TerminalEvents
}

rectangle "Frontend projection" as Projection {
  component "User turn" as UserTurn
  component "Streaming assistant turn" as AssistantTurn
  component "Expandable activity card" as ActivityCard
  component "Session and composer state" as SessionState
}

rectangle "User controls while running" as Controls {
  component "Adjust direction\n(default)" as Adjust
  component "Queue follow-up\n(configured or one-shot inverse)" as Continue
  component "Stop" as Stop
}

UserEvent --> UserTurn : persist and render
AssistantEvents --> AssistantTurn : preview then replace with final
ToolEvents --> ActivityCard : merge lifecycle and result
TerminalEvents --> SessionState : idle, complete, or recoverable error

Adjust --> SessionState : internal steer
Continue --> SessionState : internal follow-up
Stop --> SessionState : internal abort

note bottom of ActivityCard
Successful tool details collapse by default.
Errors remain expanded with recovery guidance.
Raw payloads remain in diagnostics.
end note

note bottom of SessionState
Network loss does not replay the POST.
Reload persistent history and deduplicate
by the public event identity.

Adjust direction does not interrupt the
current model call or tool execution.
end note
@enduml
